WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.421
This is SoundX AI: SoundX and Sound Deck AI,

2
00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:06.687
merged into one music studio by Mens Mercatus.

3
00:00:06.687 --> 00:00:09.472
In the next few minutes you'll see how to use it,

4
00:00:09.472 --> 00:00:11.462
how it is built and what was added.

5
00:00:11.462 --> 00:00:13.537
Then we look at JobNet.

6
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:15.777
Quick start.

7
00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:19.977
Open SoundX AI in the browser and pick SoundX Arranger in the sidebar.

8
00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:22.510
Press Demo to load a four-part arrangement,

9
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.277
then press Play in the header.

10
00:00:24.277 --> 00:00:27.458
That one transport drives whichever engine you are looking at,

11
00:00:27.458 --> 00:00:28.690
and the tempo is shared.

12
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.952
Switch to the pads and the drum deck plays instead.

13
00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:34.352
Only one engine plays at a time.

14
00:00:35.122 --> 00:00:38.332
Open the God Mode hub: sixty cards across three waves,

15
00:00:38.332 --> 00:00:40.897
from prompt-to-arrangement to session tools.

16
00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:43.495
The AI Producer takes plain commands,

17
00:00:43.495 --> 00:00:45.321
like add drums or BPM 132,

18
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:47.709
and writes clips with local rules.

19
00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:49.709
There is no cloud model.

20
00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:52.706
To use a phone as pads or a mic,

21
00:00:52.706 --> 00:00:53.920
choose Pair Phone.

22
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.645
The studio joins its own room on the existing public relay.

23
00:00:57.645 --> 00:01:01.399
Behind the six-character code, the relay room name carries an SXA

24
00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:05.383
prefix, so it never collides with SoundX deck or SoundX Studio rooms.

25
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:08.320
Save keeps the whole project in this browser.

26
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.438
Export writes one SoundX AI file,

27
00:01:10.438 --> 00:01:14.995
and Import also opens older Sound Deck AI projects and SoundX sessions.

28
00:01:15.754 --> 00:01:17.504
How it is built.

29
00:01:17.504 --> 00:01:20.829
The shell is React, built with Vite and Tailwind.

30
00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:23.450
Two Web Audio engines sit under one transport:

31
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.641
the Sound Deck drum engine and the SoundX studio engine.

32
00:01:26.641 --> 00:01:30.129
SoundX's original JavaScript modules are imported natively,

33
00:01:30.129 --> 00:01:33.616
with no iframes, and their styles are scoped and re-themed.

34
00:01:33.616 --> 00:01:37.174
On-device AI modules handle tempo, key and chord analysis,

35
00:01:37.174 --> 00:01:40.916
hum to MIDI, and mix and mastering checks inside the browser.

36
00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:44.021
A plugin rack hosts original effects and instruments,

37
00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:47.829
and the sample packs are synthesized in code and released as CC0.

38
00:01:47.829 --> 00:01:50.729
The static web build runs without a server.

39
00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:53.806
The desktop build adds a Node server for the local phone

40
00:01:53.806 --> 00:01:55.729
remote and optional cloud features.

41
00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.784
What came across from Sound Deck AI:

42
00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:01.469
the AI hub, the Top 20 AI wave in AI Plus,

43
00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:04.538
and the Mercatus Lab tools, including Resonator,

44
00:02:04.538 --> 00:02:07.031
Audio Desk, the Prompt and Lyric Forge,

45
00:02:07.031 --> 00:02:09.219
Platform Master and the DAW bridge.

46
00:02:09.219 --> 00:02:12.428
From SoundX: the Pattern, Piano and Song views,

47
00:02:12.428 --> 00:02:14.749
the God Mode hub, the Ghost layer,

48
00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:18.094
Night Shift, version snapshots and phone pairing.

49
00:02:18.094 --> 00:02:21.594
All twenty-two themes, and the light and dark switch,

50
00:02:21.594 --> 00:02:22.519
now skin both.

51
00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.515
Now, JobNet.

52
00:02:25.515 --> 00:02:30.514
JobNet is Katlego's career pipeline: a set of scheduled agent routines

53
00:02:30.514 --> 00:02:34.727
that find roles, tailor applications and watch for replies.

54
00:02:34.727 --> 00:02:37.902
A human stays in charge of every send.

55
00:02:38.674 --> 00:02:41.968
A daily scrape reads LinkedIn and Glassdoor only,

56
00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:45.549
and writes a shortlist with the reason each role fits.

57
00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:49.612
A tailor run reorders and emphasises the real CV for each

58
00:02:49.612 --> 00:02:52.749
role, with no invented employers or metrics,

59
00:02:52.749 --> 00:02:54.674
and prepares a cover email.

60
00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:59.986
Applications are saved as Gmail drafts addressed to Katlego's own inbox.

61
00:02:59.986 --> 00:03:04.624
Nothing is sent automatically, and nothing applies on its own.

62
00:03:04.624 --> 00:03:07.942
An inbox watch sorts new recruiter replies,

63
00:03:07.942 --> 00:03:10.411
rejections and acknowledgements.

64
00:03:10.411 --> 00:03:14.272
A twenty-four hour nudge then lists any reply that has waited

65
00:03:14.272 --> 00:03:15.981
more than a day for action,

66
00:03:15.981 --> 00:03:19.336
as a reminder draft that is never sent automatically.

67
00:03:20.098 --> 00:03:22.898
The run records are kept on disk.

68
00:03:22.898 --> 00:03:27.020
For example, the noon run on the twentieth of October reviewed

69
00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.611
ninety-seven LinkedIn cards and shortlisted ten roles,

70
00:03:30.611 --> 00:03:33.935
while Glassdoor was blocked by a Cloudflare check.

71
00:03:33.935 --> 00:03:37.439
In the portfolio, the JobNet page is now JobNet AI:

72
00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:41.768
a read-only showcase that runs its machine learning live in the

73
00:03:41.768 --> 00:03:45.135
visitor's browser, with no access to any mailbox.

74
00:03:45.898 --> 00:03:48.823
Here is what was added to JobNet.

75
00:03:48.823 --> 00:03:52.125
Eight AI features: job matching with a fit score,

76
00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:55.898
using an on-device MiniLM model with a keyword fallback;

77
00:03:55.898 --> 00:03:59.199
a skill-gap radar; a prioritiser that weighs fit,

78
00:03:59.199 --> 00:04:03.579
freshness and salary; a cover letter preview built only from real

79
00:04:03.579 --> 00:04:05.668
CV facts and marked as a draft;

80
00:04:05.668 --> 00:04:07.891
an outcome model; a reply sorter;

81
00:04:07.891 --> 00:04:11.260
a freelance lead finder; and a pipeline dashboard.

82
00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:16.002
The outcome model is a small logistic regression trained on twenty-five

83
00:04:16.002 --> 00:04:18.073
of Katlego's real applications.

84
00:04:18.073 --> 00:04:22.043
Only its coefficients ship, and the page says plainly that it

85
00:04:22.043 --> 00:04:24.060
is no better than guessing yet.

86
00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:29.210
The listings, leads and emails on the page are labelled sample data.

87
00:04:29.962 --> 00:04:32.374
That's SoundX AI and JobNet.

88
00:04:32.374 --> 00:04:35.449
Both are in the Mens Mercatus portfolio preview.

